course: dictionary
lesson: 846
title: Best: one word, many jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Best is a small word that does lots of jobs, so look at the words next to it. «Maya is the best player in the team.» Here best means better than all the others, so it tells you about Maya.
explain: «Do what works best.» Here best tells you how something is done. It means in the most suitable way. Check by swapping in "most suitable" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «I did my best to keep you from it.» Your best means the most you can do. Phrases like best friend and all the best also use best, so read the words around it to find its meaning.
fact: Best can be an adjective: «the best player» means better than all the others.
fact: Best can be an adverb: «Do what works best» means in the most suitable way.
fact: Best can be a noun: «do your best» means the most you can do.
fact: «Best friend» means the friend you like most.
fact: «At best» means at the very most, and «make the best of» means use something as well as you can.
exercise: «Maya is the best player in the team.» What does best mean here? | Most suitable for the job | Lowest and slowest | Most liked of everyone | *Better than all the others
exercise: «Do what works best.» What does best mean here? | Better than all the others | Very loudly | *In the most suitable way | Most liked
exercise: «I did my best to keep you from it.» What does your best mean? | *The most you can do | Last of all | A friend you like | The worst you can do
test: What does best mean in «Ella is my best friend.»? | Worst | Slowest | Tallest | *Most liked of all
test: What does «at best» mean in «We will finish at best by Friday.»? | *At the very most | Never | At the very least | In the middle of the week
exam: Which meaning of best fits «Make the best of a rainy day»? | Choose the most expensive | Forget it quickly | Wish the rain away | *Use it as well as you can
